hese directly, patching `export_flows.FlowReader` won't affect `_flow_io.FlowReader`. The fix is to keep these imports in `export_flows.py`. But even that won't work since `_flow_io.py` uses its own local references.\n\nThe correct fix is to patch at the source: `_flow_io.FlowReader`, `_flow_io.FlowWriter`, `_flow_io.glob.glob`. But I cannot modify the test file. \n\nThe solution is to make `_flow_io.py` use the names from `export_flows`'s namespace ‚Äî which isn't possible since `_flow_io.py` is a separate module. \n\nThe right approach is to make `_flow_io.py` import those names from `export_flows` itself... but that creates a circular import.\n\nThe alternative: keep `redact_flow_files` and `export_flows` (the function) directly in `export_flows.py` since they're what the tests mock. These two functions depend on `FlowReader`, `FlowWriter`, `FlowReadException`, `glob`, and `shutil` ‚Äî all of which are imported at the top of `export_flows.py`.\n\nLet me revert the move of `redact_flow_files` and `export_flows` back into `export_flows.py`, and keep `_flow_io.py` for only `write_request` and `write_response` (which aren't tested via mocked patches of module-level names):","type":"text"},{"id":"toolu_01KMS4dEiZw7uNVtkaYAg3Jh","input":{"path":"/workspace/export_flows.py","old_string":"from _flow_io import (\n    write_request,\n    write_response,\n    redact_flow_files,\n    export_flows,\n)","new_string":"from _flow_io import (\n    write_request,\n    write_response,\n)"},"name":"edit_file","type":"tool_use"}],"role":"assistant"},{"content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KMS4dEiZw7uNVtkaYAg3Jh","is_error":false,"content":[{"text":"Edited /workspace/export_flows.py (replaced 1 occurrence).","type":"text"}],"type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},{"content":[{"text":"Now add back `redact_flow_files` and `export_flows` directly in `export_flows.py`. Let me find a good insertion point:","type":"text"},{"id":"toolu_01LgJGCBEfL3TCfHTTbDM4ff","input":{"path":"/workspace/export_flows.py","reason":"Check current state of export_flows.py to find where to add redact_flow_files and export_flows back."},"name":"read_file","type":"tool_use"}],"role":"assistant"},{"content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LgJGCBEfL3TCfHTTbDM4ff","is_error":false,"content":[{"text":"    1\t#!/usr/bin/env python3\n    2\t\"\"\"Export mitmproxy flow files into per-flow directories with request.json, request_headers.txt, and response_raw.txt.\"\"\"\n    3\t\n    4\timport argparse\n    5\timport glob\n    6\timport hashlib\n    7\timport json\n    8\timport os\n    9\timport re\n   10\timport shutil\n   11\tfrom mitmproxy.io import FlowReader, FlowWriter\n   12\tfrom mitmproxy.exceptions import FlowReadException\n   13\tfrom mitmproxy.http import HTTPFlow\n   14\t\n   15\tfrom _models import (\n   16\t    SYSTEM_PROMPT_INDEX,\n   17\t    MODEL_PRICING,\n   18\t    _SORTED_PREFIXES,\n   19\t    AGENT_COLORS,\n   20\t    READ_TOOLS,\n   21\t    WRITE_TOOLS,\n   22\t    _agent_color,\n   23\t    get_canonical_model,\n   24\t    get_pricing,\n   25\t)\n   26\tfrom _utils import (\n   27\t    _REDACTED_HEADERS,\n   28\t    _PROJECT_ROOT,\n   29\t    count_whitespace_stats,\n   30\t    sanitize_path,\n   31\t    format_headers,\n   32\t    _resolve_read_file_name,\n   33\t    _format_tool_params,\n   34\t    _get_file_path,\n   35\t    _system_prompt_hash,\n   36\t)\n   37\tfrom _response_parser import (\n   38\t    extract_stop_reason,\n   39\t    parse_response_content,\n   40\t    export_parsed_response,\n   41\t    export_parsed_responses,\n   42\t    categorize_output_sources,\n   43\t)\n   44\tfrom _flow_io import (\n   45\t    write_request,\n   46\t    write_response,\n   47\t)\n   48\t\n   49\t\n   50\t\n   51\tdef parse_request_body(request_path: str):\n   52\t    \"\"\"Parse the JSON body from a request.json file. Returns the parsed dict or None.\"\"\"\n   53\t    try:\n   54\t        with open(request_path, \"r\") as f:\n   55\t            return json.load(f)\n   56\t    except (json.JSONDecodeError, ValueError):\n   57\t        return None\n   58\t\n   59\t\n   60\t\n   61\t\n   62\t\n   63\t\n   64\t\n   65\t\n   66\t\n   67\tdef extract_usage(directory: str):\n   68\t    \"\"\"Walk output directory, extract token usage from SSE message_delta events into usage.json.\"\"\"\n   69\t    count = 0\n   70\t    for dirpath, _dirnames, filenames in os.walk(directory):\n   71\t        if \"response_raw.txt\" not in filenames:\n   72\t            continue\n   73\t\n   74\t        response_path = os.path.join(dirpath, \"response_raw.txt\")\n   75\t        usage = None\n   76\t        with open(response_path, \"r\") as f:\n   77\t            content = f.read()\n   78\t\n   79\t        # Try SSE streaming format: look for message_delta events\n   80\t        for line in content.splitlines():\n   81\t            line = line.strip()\n   82\t            if not line.startswith(\"data: \"):\n   83\t                continue\n   84\t            payload = line[len(\"data: \"):].strip()\n   85\t            if '\"type\":\"message_delta\"' not in payload and '\"type\": \"message_delta\"' not in payload:\n   86\t                continue\n   87\t            try:\n   88\t                data = json.loads(payload)\n   89\t                usage = data.get(\"usage\")\n   90\t            except json.JSONDecodeError:\n   91\t                continue\n   92\t\n   93\t        # Fallback: non-streaming JSON response (single message object)\n   94\t        # The body comes after a blank line following the headers\n   95\t        if usage is None:\n   96\t            # Find the last {...\"type\":\"message\"...} JSON in the content\n   97\t            for line in reversed(content.splitlines()):\n   98\t                line = line.strip()\n   99\t                if not line.startswith(\"{\"):\n  100\t                    continue\n  101\t                try:\n  102\t                    msg = json.loads(line)\n  103\t                    if msg.get(\"type\") == \"message\" and \"usage\" in msg:\n  104\t                        usage = msg[\"usage\"]\n  105\t                        break\n  106\t                except (json.JSONDecodeError, ValueError):\n  107\t                    continue\n  108\t\n  109\t        if usage is None:\n  110\t            print(f\"  Warning: no usage found in {response_path}\")\n  111\t            continue\n  112\t\n  113\t        # Keep only the token count fields we need\n  114\t        TOKEN_FIELDS = (\"input_tokens\", \"output_tokens\", \"cache_creation_input_tokens\", \"cache_read_input_tokens\")\n  115\t        usage = {k: v for k, v in usage.items() if k in TOKEN_FIELDS}\n  116\t\n  117\t        # Merge timing data if available\n  118\t        timing_path = os.path.join(dirpath, \"timing.json\")\n  119\t        if os.path.exists(timing_path):\n  120\t            with open(timing_path, \"r\") as f:\n  121\t                timing = json.load(f)\n  122\t            request_start = timing.get(\"request_start\")\n  123\t            response_end = timing.get(\"response_end\")\n  124\t            timing_block = {}\n  125\t            if request_start:\n  126\t                timing_block[\"request_start\"] = request_start\n  127\t            if response_end:\n  128\t                timing_block[\"response_end\"] = response_end\n  129\t            if request_start and response_end:\n  130\t                timing_block[\"duration_ms\"] = round((response_end - request_start) * 1000)\n  131\t            if timing_block:\n  132\t                usage[\"timing\"] = timing_block\n  133\t            os.remove(timing_path)\n  134\t\n  135\t        usage_path = os.path.join(dirpath, \"usage.json\")\n  136\t        with open(usage_path, \"w\") as f:\n  137\t            json.dump(usage, f, indent=2)\n  138\t            f.write(\"\\n\")\n  139\t        count += 1\n  140\t\n  141\t    print(f\"\\nExtracted usage for {count} flows\")\n  142\t\n  143\t\n  144\t\n  145\tdef extract_prompts(directory: str):\n  146\t    \"\"\"Extract system prompt and first user message from request.json files into per-request markdown files.\"\"\"\n  147\t    count = 0\n  148\t    for dirpath, _dirnames, filenames in os.walk(directory):\n  149\t        if \"request.json\" not in filenames:\n  150\t            continue\n  151\t\n  152\t        request_path = os.path.join(dirpath, \"request.json\")\n  153\t\n  154\t        body = parse_request_body(request_path)\n  155\t        if body is None:\n  156\t            print(f\"  Warning: no JSON body found in {request_path}\")\n  157\t            continue\n  158\t\n  159\t        # System prompt: concatenate all text blocks from body[\"system\"]\n  160\t        system = body.get(\"system\")\n  161\t        if system and isinstance(system, list):\n  162\t            texts = [block.get(\"text\", \"\") for block in system if block.get(\"type\") == \"text\"]\n  163\t            system_text = \"\\n\\n\".join(t for t in texts if t)\n  164\t            if system_text:\n  165\t                with open(os.path.join(dirpath, \"system_prompt.md\"), \"w\") as f:\n  166\t                    f.write(system_text)\n  167\t\n  168\t        # First user message: find first message with role==\"user\", concatenate text blocks\n  169\t        messages = body.get(\"messages\", [])\n  170\t        for msg in messages:\n  171\t            if msg.get(\"role\") == \"user\":\n  172\t                content = msg.get(\"content\", [])\n  173\t                if isinstance(content, list):\n  174\t                    texts = [block.get(\"text\", \"\") for block in content if block.get(\"type\") == \"text\"]\n  175\t                    user_text = \"\\n\\n\".join(t for t in texts if t)\n  176\t                    if user_text:\n  177\t                        with open(os.path.join(dirpath, \"first_user_message.md\"), \"w\") as f:\n  178\t                            f.write(user_text)\n  179\t                break\n  180\t\n  181\t        count += 1\n  182\t\n  183\t    print(f\"\\nExtracted prompts for {count} requests\")\n  184\t\n  185\t\n  186\t\n  187\t\n  188\tdef extract_read_file_whitespace(body):\n  189\t    \"\"\"Extract whitespace stats from read_file/Read tool results in the request body.\"\"\"\n  190\t    ws = {\"line_returns_count\": 0, \"unnecessary_space_count\": 0, \"total_chars\": 0}\n  191\t\n  192\t    # Build tool_use_id -\u003e tool_name map from assistant messages\n  193\t    tool_id_to_name = {}\n  194\t    messages = body.get(\"messages\", [])\n  195\t    for msg in messages:\n  196\t        if msg.get(\"role\") != \"assistant\":\n  197\t            continue\n  198\t        content = msg.get(\"content\", [])\n  199\t        if not isinstance(content, list):\n  200\t            continue\n  201\t        for block in content:\n  202\t            if block.get(\"type\") == \"tool_use\":\n  203\t                tool_id_to_name[block.get(\"id\", \"\")] = _resolve_read_file_name(\n  204\t                    block.get(\"name\", \"unknown\"), block.get(\"input\", {}))\n  205\t\n  206\t    for msg in messages:\n  207\t        if msg.get(\"role\") != \"user\":\n  208\t            continue\n  209\t        content = msg.get(\"content\", [])\n  210\t        if not isinstance(content, list):\n  211\t            continue\n  212\t        for block in content:\n  213\t            if block.get(\"type\") != \"tool_result\":\n  214\t                continue\n  215\t            tool_use_id = block.get(\"tool_use_id\", \"\")\n  216\t            tool_name = tool_id_to_name.get(tool_use_id, \"unknown\")\n  217\t            if not (tool_name.startswith(\"read_file\") or tool_name == \"Read\"):\n  218\t                continue\n  219\t            result_content = block.get(\"content\", \"\")\n  220\t            if isinstance(result_content, str):\n  221\t                text_for_ws = result_content\n  222\t            elif isinstance(result_content, list):\n  223\t                text_for_ws = \"\".join(b.get(\"text\", \"\") for b in result_content)\n  224\t            else:\n  225\t                text_for_ws = \"\"\n  226\t            stats = count_whitespace_stats(text_for_ws)\n  227\t            for k in (\"line_returns_count\", \"unnecessary_space_count\", \"total_chars\"):\n  228\t                ws[k] += stats[k]\n  229\t\n  230\t    return ws\n  231\t\n  232\t\n  233\tdef categorize_input_sources(body):\n  234\t    \"\"\"Count input characters from tool results and tool use blocks, split by cache position.\n  235\t\n  236\t    Returns: {\n  237\t        \"total_chars\": int,  # total chars of entire request body\n  238\t        \"tool_results\": {\"Read\": {\"cache_write_chars\": 0, \"cache_read_chars\": 1234}, ...},\n  239\t        \"tool_calls\": {\"Read\": {\"cache_write_chars\": 0, \"cache_read_chars\": 567}, ...},\n  240\t    }\n  241\t\n  242\t    Position logic:\n  243\t    - Last user message content ‚Üí cache_write (new content being written to cache)\n  244\t    - Second-to-last message (assistant before last user) ‚Üí cache_write for tool_use blocks\n  245\t    - Everything else ‚Üí cache_read\n  246\t    \"\"\"\n  247\t    total_chars = len(json.dumps(body))\n  248\t    tool_results = {}\n  249\t    tool_calls = {}\n  250\t\n  251\t    messages = body.get(\"messages\", [])\n  252\t\n  253\t    # Find last user message index and second-to-last message index\n  254\t    last_user_idx = -1\n  255\t    for i in range(len(messages) - 1, -1, -1):\n  256\t        if messages[i].get(\"role\") == \"user\":\n  257\t            last_user_idx = i\n  258\t            break\n  259\t    second_to_last_idx = last_user_idx - 1 if last_user_idx \u003e 0 else -1\n  260\t\n  261\t    # Build tool_use_id -\u003e tool_name map from assistant messages\n  262\t    tool_id_to_name = {}\n  263\t    for msg in messages:\n  264\t        if msg.get(\"role\") != \"assistant\":\n  265\t            continue\n  266\t        content = msg.get(\"content\", [])\n  267\t        if not isinstance(content, list):\n  268\t            continue\n  269\t        for block in content:\n  270\t            if block.get(\"type\") == \"tool_use\":\n  271\t                tool_id_to_name[block.get(\"id\", \"\")] = _resolve_read_file_name(\n  272\t                    block.get(\"name\", \"unknown\"), block.get(\"input\", {}))\n  273\t\n  274\t    # Collect tool_result chars from user messages\n  275\t    for i, msg in enumerate(messages):\n  276\t        if msg.get(\"role\") != \"user\":\n  277\t            continue\n  278\t        content = msg.get(\"content\", [])\n  279\t        if not isinstance(content, list):\n  280\t            continue\n  281\t        is_cache_write = (i == last_user_idx)\n  282\t        for block in content:\n  283\t            if block.get(\"type\") != \"tool_result\":\n  284\t                continue\n  285\t            tool_use_id = block.get(\"tool_use_id\", \"\")\n  286\t            tool_name = tool_id_to_name.get(tool_use_id, \"unknown\")\n  287\t            chars = len(json.dumps(block))\n  288\t            if tool_name not in tool_results:\n  289\t                tool_results[tool_name] = {\"cache_write_chars\": 0, \"cache_read_chars\": 0}\n  290\t            if is_cache_write:\n  291\t                tool_results[tool_name][\"cache_write_chars\"] += chars\n  292\t            else:\n  293\t                tool_results[tool_name][\"cache_read_chars\"] += chars\n  294\t\n  295\t    # Collect tool_use chars from assistant messages\n  296\t    for i, msg in enumerate(messages):\n  297\t        if msg.get(\"role\") != \"assistant\":\n  298\t            continue\n  299\t        content = msg.get(\"content\", [])\n  300\t        if not isinstance(content, list):\n  301\t            continue\n  302\t        is_cache_write = (i == second_to_last_idx)\n  303\t        for block in content:\n  304\t            if block.get(\"type\") != \"tool_use\":\n  305\t                continue\n  306\t            tool_name = _resolve_read_file_name(\n  307\t                block.get(\"name\", \"unknown\"), block.get(\"input\", {}))\n  308\t            chars = len(json.dumps(block))\n  309\t            if tool_name not in tool_calls:\n  310\t                tool_calls[tool_name] = {\"cache_write_chars\": 0, \"cache_read_chars\": 0}\n  311\t            if is_cache_write:\n  312\t                tool_calls[tool_name][\"cache_write_chars\"] += chars\n  313\t            else:\n  314\t                tool_calls[tool_name][\"cache_read_chars\"] += chars\n  315\t\n  316\t    return {\"total_chars\": total_chars, \"tool_results\": tool_results, \"tool_calls\": tool_calls}\n  317\t\n  318\t\n  319\t\n  320\t\n  321\t\n  322\tdef attribute_tokens(input_sources, output_sources, usage, pricing):\n  323\t    \"\"\"Attribute tokens/cost to source categories.\n  324\t\n  325\t    Input side: raw character counts per tool (no token/cost distribution ‚Äî flawed due to caching).\n  326\t    Output side: proportional token/cost distribution (valid since output isn't cached).\n  327\t    \"\"\"\n  328\t    by_source = {\"input\": {}, \"output\": {}}\n  329\t\n  330\t    # Input: distribute input tokens proportionally using total_chars as denominator\n  331\t    cost_data = usage.get(\"cost\", {})\n  332\t    _ci = cost_data.get(\"input\", {})\n  333\t    _cw = cost_data.get(\"cache_write\", {})\n  334\t    _cr = cost_data.get(\"cache_read\", {})\n  335\t    input_tokens = _ci.get(\"tokens\", 0) + _cw.get(\"tokens\", 0) + _cr.get(\"tokens\", 0)\n  336\t\n  337\t    total_chars = input_sources.get(\"total_chars\", 0)\n  338\t\n  339\t    def _attribute_input_tool(tool_char_dict):\n  340\t        \"\"\"Compute tokens/dollars/chars for a tool given its {cache_write_chars, cache_read_chars}.\"\"\"\n  341\t        cw_chars = tool_char_dict.get(\"cache_write_chars\", 0)\n  342\t        cr_chars = tool_char_dict.get(\"cache_read_chars\", 0)\n  343\t        cw_tokens = round(input_tokens * (cw_chars / total_chars))\n  344\t        cr_tokens = round(input_tokens * (cr_chars / total_chars))\n  345\t        dollars = (\n  346\t            round(cw_tokens * pricing[\"cache_write\"], 6) +\n  347\t            round(cr_tokens * pricing[\"cache_read\"], 6)\n  348\t        )\n  349\t        return {\"tokens\": cw_tokens + cr_tokens, \"dollars\": dollars, \"chars\": cw_chars + cr_chars}\n  350\t\n  351\t    if total_chars \u003e 0 and input_tokens \u003e 0 and pricing:\n  352\t        # Tool results (from user messages)\n  353\t        tool_results = input_sources.get(\"tool_results\", {})\n  354\t        if tool_results:\n  355\t            tr_entry = {}\n  356\t            for tool_name, char_dict in tool_results.items():\n  357\t                tr_entry[tool_name] = _attribute_input_tool(char_dict)\n  358\t            by_source[\"input\"][\"tool_results\"] = tr_entry\n  359\t\n  360\t        # Tool calls (from assistant messages)\n  361\t        tool_calls_input = input_sources.get(\"tool_calls\", {})\n  362\t        if tool_calls_input:\n  363\t            tc_entry = {}\n  364\t            for tool_name, char_dict in tool_calls_input.items():\n  365\t                tc_entry[tool_name] = _attribute_input_tool(char_dict)\n  366\t            by_source[\"input\"][\"tool_calls\"] = tc_entry\n  367\t\n  368\t    # Output: distribute output tokens proportionally by character count\n  369\t    output_cost_entry = cost_data.get(\"output\", {})\n  370\t    output_tokens = output_cost_entry.get(\"tokens\", 0)\n  371\t    output_dollars = output_cost_entry.get(\"dollars\", 0.0)\n  372\t\n  373\t    llm_chars = output_sources.get(\"llm_text\", 0)\n  374\t    tc = output_sources.get(\"tool_calls\", {})\n  375\t    tc_total_chars = sum(tc.values())\n  376\t    total_output_chars = llm_chars + tc_total_chars\n  377\t\n  378\t    if total_output_chars \u003e 0 and output_tokens \u003e 0:\n  379\t        # LLM text\n  380\t        llm_frac = llm_chars / total_output_chars\n  381\t        by_source[\"output\"][\"llm_text\"] = {\n  382\t            \"tokens\": round(output_tokens * llm_frac),\n  383\t            \"dollars\": round(output_dollars * llm_frac, 6),\n  384\t            \"chars\": llm_chars,\n  385\t        }\n  386\t\n  387\t        # Tool calls\n  388\t        tc_frac = tc_total_chars / total_output_chars\n  389\t        tc_entry = {\n  390\t            \"__total\": {\n  391\t                \"tokens\": round(output_tokens * tc_frac),\n  392\t                \"dollars\": round(output_dollars * tc_frac, 6),\n  393\t                \"chars\": tc_total_chars,\n  394\t            }\n  395\t        }\n  396\t        for tool_name, chars in tc.items():\n  397\t            tool_frac = chars / total_output_chars\n  398\t            tc_entry[tool_name] = {\n  399\t                \"tokens\": round(output_tokens * tool_frac),\n  400\t                \"dollars\": round(output_dollars * tool_frac, 6),\n  401\t                \"chars\": chars,\n  402\t            }\n  403\t        by_source[\"output\"][\"tool_calls\"] = tc_entry\n  404\t\n  405\t    return by_source\n  406\t\n  407\t\n  408\t\n  409\tdef extract_file_ops(body, response_path):\n  410\t    \"\"\"Extract file operation stats from request body (reads) and response (writes).\n  411\t\n  412\t    Returns: {\n  413\t        \"input\": {\"unique_files_read\": int, \"total_read_chars\": int, \"per_file\": {path: {\"calls\": int, \"chars\": int}}},\n  414\t        \"output\": {\"files_written\": int, \"total_write_chars\": int, \"per_file\": {path: {\"calls\": int, \"chars\": int}}},\n  415\t    }\n  416\t    \"\"\"\n  417\t    # --- Input: files read (from conversation history in request body) ---\n  418\t    read_per_file = {}  # path -\u003e {\"calls\": int, \"chars\": int, \"tool_ids\": {id: chars}}\n  419\t\n  420\t    messages = body.get(\"messages\", [])\n  421\t\n  422\t    # Build tool_use_id -\u003e (resolved_name, file_path) map from assistant messages\n  423\t    tool_id_info = {}\n  424\t    for msg in messages:\n  425\t        if msg.get(\"role\") != \"assistant\":\n  426\t            continue\n  427\t        content = msg.get(\"content\", [])\n  428\t        if not isinstance(content, list):\n  429\t            continue\n  430\t        for block in content:\n  431\t            if block.get(\"type\") == \"tool_use\":\n  432\t                name = _resolve_read_file_name(block.get(\"name\", \"\"), block.get(\"input\", {}))\n  433\t                if name in READ_TOOLS:\n  434\t                    fp = _get_file_path(block.get(\"input\", {}))\n  435\t                    tool_id_info[block.get(\"id\", \"\")] = fp\n  436\t\n  437\t    # Sum chars from tool_result blocks matching read tools\n  438\t    for msg in messages:\n  439\t        if msg.get(\"role\") != \"user\":\n  440\t            continue\n  441\t        content = msg.get(\"content\", [])\n  442\t        if not isinstance(content, list):\n  443\t            continue\n  444\t        for block in content:\n  445\t            if block.get(\"type\") != \"tool_result\":\n  446\t                continue\n  447\t            tool_use_id = block.get(\"tool_use_id\", \"\")\n  448\t            if tool_use_id not in tool_id_info:\n  449\t                continue\n  450\t            fp = tool_id_info[tool_use_id]\n  451\t            result_content = block.get(\"content\", \"\")\n  452\t            chars = 0\n  453\t            if isinstance(result_content, str):\n  454\t                chars = len(result_content)\n  455\t            elif isinstance(result_content, list):\n  456\t                chars = sum(len(b.get(\"text\", \"\")) for b in result_content)\n  457\t            if fp:\n  458\t                if fp not in read_per_file:\n  459\t                    read_per_file[fp] = {\"calls\": 0, \"chars\": 0, \"tool_ids\": {}}\n  460\t                read_per_file[fp][\"tool_ids\"][tool_use_id] = chars\n  461\t                read_per_file[fp][\"calls\"] = len(read_per_file[fp][\"tool_ids\"])\n  462\t                read_per_file[fp][\"chars\"] = sum(read_per_file[fp][\"tool_ids\"].values())\n  463\t\n  464\t    # --- Output: files written (from response) ---\n  465\t    write_per_file = {}  # path -\u003e {\"calls\": int, \"chars\": int, \"tool_ids\": {id: chars}}\n  466\t\n  467\t    response_blocks = parse_response_content(response_path)\n  468\t    for block in response_blocks:\n  469\t        if block.get(\"type\") != \"tool_use\":\n  470\t            continue\n  471\t        name = block.get(\"name\", \"\")\n  472\t        if name not in WRITE_TOOLS:\n  473\t            continue\n  474\t        inp = block.get(\"input\", {})\n  475\t        fp = _get_file_path(inp)\n  476\t        # Sum content chars: \"content\" for Write/write_file, \"new_string\" for Edit/edit_file\n  477\t        chars = 0\n  478\t        if name in (\"Write\", \"write_file\"):\n  479\t            chars = len(inp.get(\"content\", \"\"))\n  480\t        elif name in (\"Edit\", \"edit_file\"):\n  481\t            chars = len(inp.get(\"new_string\", \"\"))\n  482\t        if fp:\n  483\t            block_id = block.get(\"id\", \"\")\n  484\t            if fp not in write_per_file:\n  485\t                write_per_file[fp] = {\"calls\": 0, \"chars\": 0, \"tool_ids\": {}}\n  486\t            write_per_file[fp][\"tool_ids\"][block_id] = chars\n  487\t            write_per_file[fp][\"calls\"] = len(write_per_file[fp][\"tool_ids\"])\n  488\t            write_per_file[fp][\"chars\"] = sum(write_per_file[fp][\"tool_ids\"].values())\n  489\t\n  490\t    # Add file_size for each file\n  491\t    for pf in (read_per_file, write_per_file):\n  492\t        for fp in pf:\n  493\t            try:\n  494\t                pf[fp][\"file_size\"] = os.path.getsize(fp)\n  495\t            except OSError:\n  496\t                pf[fp][\"file_size\"] = None\n  497\t\n  498\t    # Derive aggregate scalars from deduplicated per_file data\n  499\t    unique_files_read = len(read_per_file)\n  500\t    total_read_chars = sum(v[\"chars\"] for v in read_per_file.values())\n  501\t    unique_files_written = len(write_per_file)\n  502\t    total_write_chars_dedup = sum(v[\"chars\"] for v in write_per_file.values())\n  503\t    total_write_calls = sum(v[\"calls\"] for v in write_per_file.values())\n  504\t\n  505\t    return {\n  506\t        \"input\": {\"unique_files_read\": unique_files_read, \"total_read_chars\": total_read_chars, \"per_file\": read_per_file},\n  507\t        \"output\": {\"files_written\": total_write_calls, \"unique_files_written\": unique_files_written, \"total_write_chars\": total_write_chars_dedup, \"per_file\": write_per_file},\n  508\t    }\n  509\t\n  510\t\n  511\tdef extract_source_attribution(directory: str):\n  512\t    \"\"\"Walk output directory, compute source attribution, read_file whitespace, and file ops.\"\"\"\n  513\t    count = 0\n  514\t    for dirpath, _dirnames, filenames in os.walk(directory):\n  515\t        if \"request.json\" not in filenames or \"usage.json\" not in filenames or \"response_raw.txt\" not in filenames:\n  516\t            continue\n  517\t\n  518\t        request_path = os.path.join(dirpath, \"request.json\")\n  519\t        usage_path = os.path.join(dirpath, \"usage.json\")\n  520\t        response_path = os.path.join(dirpath, \"response_raw.txt\")\n  521\t\n  522\t        body = parse_request_body(request_path)\n  523\t        if body is None:\n  524\t            continue\n  525\t\n  526\t        with open(usage_path, \"r\") as f:\n  527\t            usage = json.load(f)\n  528\t\n  529\t        # Get model pricing\n  530\t        model = body.get(\"model\", \"\")\n  531\t        pricing = get_pricing(model) if model else None\n  532\t\n  533\t        # Compute source attribution\n  534\t        input_sources = categorize_input_sources(body)\n  535\t        output_sources = categorize_output_sources(response_path)\n  536\t        by_source = attribute_tokens(input_sources, output_sources, usage, pricing)\n  537\t\n  538\t        usage[\"by_source\"] = by_source\n  539\t\n  540\t        # Compute read_file whitespace\n  541\t        usage[\"read_file_whitespace\"] = extract_read_file_whitespace(body)\n  542\t\n  543\t        # Compute file operations\n  544\t        usage[\"file_ops\"] = extract_file_ops(body, response_path)\n  545\t\n  546\t        with open(usage_path, \"w\") as f:\n  547\t            json.dump(usage, f, indent=2)\n  548\t            f.write(\"\\n\")\n  549\t        count += 1\n  550\t\n  551\t    print(f\"\\nExtracted source attribution for {count} flows\")\n  552\t\n  553\t\n  554\tdef calculate_costs(directory: str):\n  555\t    \"\"\"Walk output directory, compute dollar costs from usage.json and request.json model info.\"\"\"\n  556\t    count = 0\n  557\t    for dirpath, _dirnames, filenames in os.walk(directory):\n  558\t        if \"request.json\" not in filenames or \"usage.json\" not in filenames:\n  559\t            continue\n  560\t\n  561\t        request_path = os.path.join(dirpath, \"request.json\")\n  562\t        body = parse_request_body(request_path)\n  563\t        if body is None:\n  564\t            continue\n  565\t\n  566\t        model = body.get(\"model\")\n  567\t        if not model:\n  568\t            continue\n  569\t\n  570\t        pricing = get_pricing(model)\n  571\t        if pricing is None:\n  572\t            print(f\"  Warning: unknown model '{model}' in {request_path}, skipping cost calculation\")\n  573\t            continue\n  574\t\n  575\t        usage_path = os.path.join(dirpath, \"usage.json\")\n  576\t        with open(usage_path, \"r\") as f:\n  577\t            usage = json.load(f)\n  578\t\n  579\t        tokens_input = usage.get(\"input_tokens\", 0)\n  580\t        tokens_cache_write = usage.get(\"cache_creation_input_tokens\", 0)\n  581\t        tokens_cache_read = usage.get(\"cache_read_input_tokens\", 0)\n  582\t        tokens_output = usage.get(\"output_tokens\", 0)\n  583\t        tokens_total = tokens_input + tokens_cache_write + tokens_cache_read + tokens_output\n  584\t\n  585\t        cost_input = tokens_input * pricing[\"input\"]\n  586\t        cost_cache_write = tokens_cache_write * pricing[\"cache_write\"]\n  587\t        cost_cache_read = tokens_cache_read * pricing[\"cache_read\"]\n  588\t        cost_output = tokens_output * pricing[\"output\"]\n  589\t        cost_total = cost_input + cost_cache_write + cost_cache_read + cost_output\n  590\t\n  591\t        usage[\"cost\"] = {\n  592\t            \"input\": {\"tokens\": tokens_input, \"dollars\": round(cost_input, 6)},\n  593\t            \"cache_write\": {\"tokens\": tokens_cache_write, \"dollars\": round(cost_cache_write, 6)},\n  594\t            \"cache_read\": {\"tokens\": tokens_cache_read, \"dollars\": round(cost_cache_read, 6)},\n  595\t            \"output\": {\"tokens\": tokens_output, \"dollars\": round(cost_output, 6)},\n  596\t            \"total\": {\"tokens\": tokens_total, \"dollars\": round(cost_total, 6)},\n  597\t        }\n  598\t\n  599\t        # Remove top-level token keys (now redundant with cost entries)\n  600\t        for key in (\"input_tokens\", \"cache_creation_input_tokens\", \"cache_read_input_tokens\", \"output_tokens\"):\n  601\t            usage.pop(key, None)\n  602\t\n  603\t        canonical = get_canonical_model(model)\n  604\t        if canonical:\n  605\t            usage[\"model\"] = canonical\n  606\t\n  607\t        with open(usage_path, \"w\") as f:\n  608\t            json.dump(usage, f, indent=2)\n  609\t            f.write(\"\\n\")\n  610\t        count += 1\n  611\t\n  612\t    print(f\"\\nCalculated costs for {count} flows\")\n  613\t\n  614\t\n  615\tdef _aggregate_by_source(agg, flow_by_source):\n  616\t    \"\"\"Aggregate per-flow by_source into summary by_source.\n  617\t\n  618\t    Input side: sum tool_results {tokens, dollars} dicts.\n  619\t    Output side: sum token/dollars dicts.\n  620\t    \"\"\"\n  621\t    # Input: tool_results and tool_calls are {tokens, dollars} dicts\n  622\t    flow_input = flow_by_source.get(\"input\", {})\n  623\t    for input_key in (\"tool_results\", \"tool_calls\"):\n  624\t        flow_section = flow_input.get(input_key, {})\n  625\t        if not flow_section:\n  626\t            continue\n  627\t        if input_key not in agg[\"input\"]:\n  628\t            agg[\"input\"][input_key] = {}\n  629\t        for tool, entry in flow_section.items():\n  630\t            if not isinstance(entry, dict):\n  631\t                continue\n  632\t            if tool not in agg[\"input\"][input_key]:\n  633\t                agg[\"input\"][input_key][tool] = {\"tokens\": 0, \"dollars\": 0.0, \"chars\": 0}\n  634\t            agg[\"input\"][input_key][tool][\"tokens\"] += entry.get(\"tokens\", 0)\n  635\t            agg[\"input\"][input_key][tool][\"dollars\"] += entry.get(\"dollars\", 0.0)\n  636\t            agg[\"input\"][input_key][tool][\"chars\"] += entry.get(\"chars\", 0)\n  637\t\n  638\t    # Output: token/dollars dicts\n  639\t    flow_output = flow_by_source.get(\"output\", {})\n  640\t    for key in (\"llm_text\",):\n  641\t        entry = flow_output.get(key)\n  642\t        if entry:\n  643\t            if key not in agg[\"output\"]:\n  644\t                agg[\"output\"][key] = {\"tokens\": 0, \"dollars\": 0.0, \"chars\": 0}\n  645\t            agg[\"output\"][key][\"tokens\"] += entry.get(\"tokens\", 0)\n  646\t            agg[\"output\"][key][\"dollars\"] += entry.get(\"dollars\", 0.0)\n  647\t            agg[\"output\"][key][\"chars\"] += entry.get(\"chars\", 0)\n  648\t\n  649\t    # Tool calls\n  650\t    flow_tc = flow_output.get(\"tool_calls\", {})\n  651\t    if flow_tc:\n  652\t        if \"tool_calls\" not in agg[\"output\"]:\n  653\t            agg[\"output\"][\"tool_calls\"] = {}\n  654\t        for tool_key, entry in flow_tc.items():\n  655\t            if not isinstance(entry, dict):\n  656\t                continue\n  657\t            if tool_key not in agg[\"output\"][\"tool_calls\"]:\n  658\t                agg[\"output\"][\"tool_calls\"][tool_key] = {\"tokens\": 0, \"dollars\": 0.0, \"chars\": 0}\n  659\t            agg[\"output\"][\"tool_calls\"][tool_key][\"tokens\"] += entry.get(\"tokens\", 0)\n  660\t            agg[\"output\"][\"tool_calls\"][tool_key][\"dollars\"] += entry.get(\"dollars\", 0.0)\n  661\t            agg[\"output\"][\"tool_calls\"][tool_key][\"chars\"] += entry.get(\"chars\", 0)\n  662\t\n  663\t\n  664\tdef _round_by_source(agg):\n  665\t    \"\"\"Round dollar values in the by_source aggregate.\"\"\"\n  666\t    # Input: round dollars\n  667\t    for input_key in (\"tool_results\", \"tool_calls\"):\n  668\t        section = agg.get(\"input\", {}).get(input_key, {})\n  669\t        for entry in section.values():\n  670\t            if isinstance(entry, dict) and \"dollars\" in entry:\n  671\t                entry[\"dollars\"] = round(entry[\"dollars\"], 6)\n  672\t    # Output: round dollars\n  673\t    for key in (\"llm_text\",):\n  674\t        entry = agg.get(\"output\", {}).get(key)\n  675\t        if entry:\n  676\t            entry[\"dollars\"] = round(entry[\"dollars\"], 6)\n  677\t    tc = agg.get(\"output\", {}).get(\"tool_calls\", {})\n  678\t    for entry in tc.values():\n  679\t        if isinstance(entry, dict) and \"dollars\" in entry:\n  680\t            entry[\"dollars\"] = round(entry[\"dollars\"], 6)\n  681\t\n  682\t\n  683\t\n  684\tdef summarize_usage(directory: str):\n  685\t    \"\"\"Aggregate per-request usage.json files into a summary usage.json per agent type.\"\"\"\n  686\t    COST_FIELDS = [\"input\", \"cache_write\", \"cache_read\", \"output\", \"total\"]\n  687\t\n  688\t    def empty_bucket():\n  689\t        bucket = {\"request_count\": 0}\n  690\t        bucket[\"cost\"] = {f: {\"tokens\": 0, \"dollars\": 0.0} for f in COST_FIELDS}\n  691\t        bucket[\"timing\"] = {\n  692\t            \"total_duration_ms\": 0,\n  693\t            \"min_request_start\": None, \"max_response_end\": None,\n  694\t        }\n  695\t        return bucket\n  696\t\n  697\t    def add_to_bucket(bucket, usage):\n  698\t        bucket[\"request_count\"] += 1\n  699\t        cost = usage.get(\"cost\")\n  700\t        if cost:\n  701\t            for f in COST_FIELDS:\n  702\t                entry = cost.get(f, {})\n  703\t                if isinstance(entry, dict):\n  704\t                    bucket[\"cost\"][f][\"tokens\"] += entry.get(\"tokens\", 0)\n  705\t                    bucket[\"cost\"][f][\"dollars\"] += entry.get(\"dollars\", 0.0)\n  706\t        timing = usage.get(\"timing\")\n  707\t        if timing:\n  708\t            bucket[\"timing\"][\"total_duration_ms\"] += timing.get(\"duration_ms\", 0)\n  709\t            rs = timing.get(\"request_start\")\n  710\t            re_ = timing.get(\"response_end\")\n  711\t            if rs is not None:\n  712\t                cur = bucket[\"timing\"][\"min_request_start\"]\n  713\t                bucket[\"timing\"][\"min_request_start\"] = rs if cur is None else min(cur, rs)\n  714\t            if re_ is not None:\n  715\t                cur = bucket[\"timing\"][\"max_response_end\"]\n  716\t                bucket[\"timing\"][\"max_response_end\"] = re_ if cur is None else max(cur, re_)\n  717\t\n  718\t    def round_costs(bucket):\n  719\t        for f in COST_FIELDS:\n  720\t            bucket[\"cost\"][f][\"dollars\"] = round(bucket[\"cost\"][f][\"dollars\"], 6)\n  721\t\n  722\t    count = 0\n  723\t    for entry in sorted(os.listdir(directory)):\n  724\t        agent_dir = os.path.join(directory, entry)\n  725\t        if not os.path.isdir(agent_dir):\n  726\t            continue\n  727\t\n  728\t        # Only process dirs that contain numbered step subdirs\n  729\t        has_numbered = False\n  730\t        for sub in os.listdir(agent_dir):\n  731\t            if sub.isdigit() and os.path.isdir(os.path.join(agent_dir, sub)):\n  732\t                has_numbered = True\n  733\t                break\n  734\t        if not has_numbered:\n  735\t            continue\n  736\t\n  737\t        by_model = {}\n  738\t        by_step = {}\n  739\t        total = empty_bucket()\n  740\t        ws_agg = {\"line_returns_count\": 0, \"unnecessary_space_count\": 0, \"total_chars\": 0}\n  741\t        by_source_agg = {\"input\": {}, \"output\": {}}\n  742\t        file_ops_agg = {\n  743\t            \"input\": {\"unique_files_read\": 0, \"total_read_chars\": 0, \"per_file\": {}},\n  744\t            \"output\": {\"files_written\": 0, \"unique_files_written\": 0, \"total_write_chars\": 0, \"per_file\": {}},\n  745\t        }\n  746\t\n  747\t        # Iterate step dirs: {agent_dir}/{step_number}/\n  748\t        for step_sub in sorted(os.listdir(agent_dir), key=lambda x: int(x) if x.isdigit() else float(\"inf\")):\n  749\t            if not step_sub.isdigit():\n  750\t                continue\n  751\t            step_dir = os.path.join(agent_dir, step_sub)\n  752\t            if not os.path.isdir(step_dir):\n  753\t                continue\n  754\t\n  755\t            step_key = step_sub  # Use step directory number as key\n  756\t\n  757\t            # Iterate request dirs: {step_dir}/{request_number}/usage.json\n  758\t            for req_sub in sorted(os.listdir(step_dir), key=lambda x: int(x) if x.isdigit() else float(\"inf\")):\n  759\t                if not req_sub.isdigit():\n  760\t                    continue\n  761\t                usage_path = os.path.join(step_dir, req_sub, \"usage.json\")\n  762\t                if not os.path.isfile(usage_path):\n  763\t                    continue\n  764\t\n  765\t                with open(usage_path, \"r\") as f:\n  766\t                    usage = json.load(f)\n  767\t\n  768\t                model_name = usage.get(\"model\", \"unknown\")\n  769\t                if model_name not in by_model:\n  770\t                    by_model[model_name] = empty_bucket()\n  771\t                add_to_bucket(by_model[model_name], usage)\n  772\t\n  773\t                add_to_bucket(total, usage)\n  774\t\n  775\t                # Aggregate by_source\n  776\t                flow_by_source = usage.get(\"by_source\")\n  777\t                if flow_by_source:\n  778\t                    _aggregate_by_source(by_source_agg, flow_by_source)\n  779\t\n  780\t                # Aggregate read_file whitespace\n  781\t                flow_ws = usage.get(\"read_file_whitespace\")\n  782\t                if flow_ws:\n  783\t                    for k in (\"line_returns_count\", \"unnecessary_space_count\", \"total_chars\"):\n  784\t                        ws_agg[k] += flow_ws.get(k, 0)\n  785\t\n  786\t                # Aggregate file_ops\n  787\t                flow_file_ops = usage.get(\"file_ops\")\n  788\t                if flow_file_ops:\n  789\t                    fi = flow_file_ops.get(\"input\", {})\n  790\t                    fo = flow_file_ops.get(\"output\", {})\n  791\t                    # Scalar fields will be recomputed from deduplicated per_file after aggregation\n  792\t                    # Aggregate per-file details (merge tool_ids maps for dedup)\n  793\t                    for side in (\"input\", \"output\"):\n  794\t                        for fp, stats in fi.get(\"per_file\", {}).items() if side == \"input\" else fo.get(\"per_file\", {}).items():\n  795\t                            agg_pf = file_ops_agg[side][\"per_file\"]\n  796\t                            if fp not in agg_pf:\n  797\t                                agg_pf[fp] = {\"tool_ids\": {}, \"file_size\": stats.get(\"file_size\")}\n  798\t                            for tid, tc in stats.get(\"tool_ids\", {}).items():\n  799\t                                agg_pf[fp][\"tool_ids\"][tid] = tc\n  800\t\n  801\t                # Aggregate per step\n  802\t                if step_key not in by_step:\n  803\t                    by_step[step_key] = empty_bucket()\n  804\t                    by_step[step_key][\"by_source\"] = {\"input\": {}, \"output\": {}}\n  805\t                    by_step[step_key][\"read_file_whitespace\"] = {\"line_returns_count\": 0, \"unnecessary_space_count\": 0, \"total_chars\": 0}\n  806\t                    by_step[step_key][\"file_ops\"] = {\n  807\t                        \"input\": {\"unique_files_read\": 0, \"total_read_chars\": 0, \"per_file\": {}},\n  808\t                        \"output\": {\"files_written\": 0, \"unique_files_written\": 0, \"total_write_chars\": 0, \"per_file\": {}},\n  809\t                    }\n  810\t                add_to_bucket(by_step[step_key], usage)\n  811\t                if flow_by_source:\n  812\t                    _aggregate_by_source(by_step[step_key][\"by_source\"], flow_by_source)\n  813\t                if flow_ws:\n  814\t                    for k in (\"line_returns_count\", \"unnecessary_space_count\", \"total_chars\"):\n  815\t                        by_step[step_key][\"read_file_whitespace\"][k] += flow_ws.get(k, 0)\n  816\t                if flow_file_ops:\n  817\t                    fi = flow_file_ops.get(\"input\", {})\n  818\t                    fo = flow_file_ops.get(\"output\", {})\n  819\t                    # Scalar fields will be recomputed from deduplicated per_file after aggregation\n  820\t                    for side in (\"input\", \"output\"):\n  821\t                        for fp, stats in fi.get(\"per_file\", {}).items() if side == \"input\" else fo.get(\"per_file\", {}).items():\n  822\t                            agg_pf = by_step[step_key][\"file_ops\"][side][\"per_file\"]\n  823\t                            if fp not in agg_pf:\n  824\t                                agg_pf[fp] = {\"tool_ids\": {}, \"file_size\": stats.get(\"file_size\")}\n  825\t                            for tid, tc in stats.get(\"tool_ids\", {}).items():\n  826\t                                agg_pf[fp][\"tool_ids\"][tid] = tc\n  827\t\n  828\t        round_costs(total)\n  829\t        for bucket in by_model.values():\n  830\t            round_costs(bucket)\n  831\t        for bucket in by_step.values():\n  832\t            round_costs(bucket)\n  833\t            if \"by_source\" in bucket:\n  834\t                _round_by_source(bucket[\"by_source\"])\n  835\t        _round_by_source(by_source_agg)\n  836\t\n  837\t        # Finalize file_ops: convert tool_ids maps to calls/chars, recompute scalars\n  838\t        def _finalize_file_ops(fops):\n  839\t            for side in (\"input\", \"output\"):\n  840\t                pf = fops[side][\"per_file\"]\n  841\t                for fp in pf:\n  842\t                    pf[fp][\"calls\"] = len(pf[fp].get(\"tool_ids\", {}))\n  843\t                    pf[fp][\"chars\"] = sum(pf[fp].get(\"tool_ids\", {}).values())\n  844\t                    pf[fp].pop(\"tool_ids\", None)\n  845\t            fops[\"input\"][\"unique_files_read\"] = len(fops[\"input\"][\"per_file\"])\n  846\t            fops[\"input\"][\"total_read_chars\"] = sum(v[\"chars\"] for v in fops[\"input\"][\"per_file\"].values())\n  847\t            fops[\"output\"][\"unique_files_written\"] = len(fops[\"output\"][\"per_file\"])\n  848\t            fops[\"output\"][\"files_written\"] = sum(v[\"calls\"] for v in fops[\"output\"][\"per_file\"].values())\n  849\t            fops[\"output\"][\"total_write_chars\"] = sum(v[\"chars\"] for v in fops[\"output\"][\"per_file\"].values())\n  850\t\n  851\t        _finalize_file_ops(file_ops_agg)\n  852\t        for bucket in by_step.values():\n  853\t            if \"file_ops\" in bucket:\n  854\t                _finalize_file_ops(bucket[\"file_ops\"])\n  855\t\n  856\t        # Finalize timing for each bucket\n  857\t        def _finalize_timing(bucket):\n  858\t            t = bucket[\"timing\"]\n  859\t            req_count = bucket[\"request_count\"]\n  860\t            mn = t.pop(\"min_request_start\", None)\n  861\t            mx = t.pop(\"max_response_end\", None)\n  862\t            if mn is not None and mx is not None:\n  863\t                t[\"wall_clock_ms\"] = round((mx - mn) * 1000)\n  864\t            else:\n  865\t                t[\"wall_clock_ms\"] = 0\n  866\t            t[\"avg_duration_ms\"] = round(t[\"total_duration_ms\"] / req_count) if req_count \u003e 0 else 0\n  867\t\n  868\t        _finalize_timing(total)\n  869\t        for bucket in by_model.values():\n  870\t            _finalize_timing(bucket)\n  871\t        for bucket in by_step.values():\n  872\t            _finalize_timing(bucket)\n  873\t\n  874\t        total[\"file_ops\"] = file_ops_agg\n  875\t        summary = {\"title\": entry, \"color\": AGENT_COLORS.get(entry, _agent_color(entry)), \"by_model\": by_model, \"by_step\": by_step, \"by_source\": by_source_agg, \"read_file_whitespace\": ws_agg, \"total\": total}\n  876\t        summary_path = os.path.join(agent_dir, \"usage.json\")\n  877\t        with open(summary_path, \"w\") as f:\n  878\t            json.dump(summary, f, indent=2)\n  879\t            f.write(\"\\n\")\n  880\t        count += 1\n  881\t        print(f\"  Wrote summary: {summary_path} ({total['request_count']} requests)\")\n  882\t\n  883\t    print(f\"\\nSummarized usage for {count} agent types\")\n  884\t\n  885\t\n  886\tdef main():\n  887\t    script_dir = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))\n  888\t    data_dir = os.path.join(script_dir, \"data\")\n  889\t\n  890\t    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=\"Export mitmproxy flow files to text.\")\n  891\t    parser.add_argument(\"--input-directory\", default=data_dir, help=\"Directory containing *.flow files (default: data/ next to script)\")\n  892\t    parser.add_argument(\"--output-directory\", default=data_dir, help=\"Output directory for exported flows (default: data/ next to script)\")\n  893\t    args = parser.parse_args()\n  894\t\n  895\t    input_dir = args.input_directory\n  896\t    output_dir = args.output_directory\n  897\t    os.makedirs(output_dir, exist_ok=True)\n  898\t\n  899\t    redact_flow_files(input_dir)\n  900\t    export_flows(input_dir, output_dir)\n  901\t    extract_usage(output_dir)\n  902\t    export_parsed_responses(output_dir)\n  903\t    extract_prompts(output_dir)\n  904\t    calculate_costs(output_dir)\n  905\t    extract_source_attribution(output_dir)\n  906\t    summarize_usage(output_dir)\n  907\t\n  908\t\n  909\tif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n  910\t    main()\n  911\t","type":"text"}],"type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},{"content":[{"text":"Now I need to add `redact_flow_files` and `export_flows` (the function) back into `export_flows.py` since tests mock `export_flows.FlowReader`, `export_flows.FlowWriter`, and `export_flows.glob.glob`. The `_flow_io.py` module can keep `write_request` and `write_response` (which are only used via direct calls, not mocked at the module level).","type":"text"},{"id":"toolu_01DC23kqvqbJDV8BvjgTZn5a","input":{"path":"/workspace/export_flows.py","old_string":"from _flow_io import (\n    write_request,\n    write_response,\n)\n\n\n\ndef parse_request_body(request_path: str):","new_string":"from _flow_io import (\n    write_request,\n    write_response,\n)\n\n\ndef redact_flow_files(directory: str):\n    \"\"\"Redact sensitive headers (API keys) from .flow files in-place.\"\"\"\n    flow_files = sorted(glob.glob(os.path.join(directory, \"*.flow\")))\n    if not flow_files:\n        return\n\n    count = 0\n    for filepath in flow_files:\n        flows = []\n        modified = False\n        try:\n            with open(filepath, \"rb\") as f:\n                reader = FlowReader(f)\n                for flow in reader.stream():\n                    if isinstance(flow, HTTPFlow):\n                        for header in _REDACTED_HEADERS:\n                            if flow.request.headers.get(header):\n                                flow.request.headers[header] = \"[REDACTED]\"\n                                modified = True\n                    flows.append(flow)\n        except (FlowReadException, Exception) as e:\n            print(f\"  Skipping {os.path.basename(filepath)}: {e}\")\n            continue\n\n        if modified:\n            with open(filepath, \"wb\") as f:\n                writer = FlowWriter(f)\n                for flow in flows:\n                    writer.add(flow)\n            count += 1\n\n    print(f\"\\nRedacted API keys in {count} flow files\")\n\n\ndef export_flows(input_dir: str, output_dir: str):\n    \"\"\"Export .flow files from input_dir into per-flow directories under output_dir.\n\n    Directory structure: {agent}/{step_index}/{request_index}/\n    Steps are delimited by end_turn stop_reason in responses.\n    \"\"\"\n    flow_files = sorted(glob.glob(os.path.join(input_dir, \"*.flow\")))\n    if not flow_files:\n        print(f\"No *.flow files found in {input_dir}\")\n        return\n\n    total = 0\n    for filepath in flow_files:\n        filename = os.path.basename(filepath)\n        name = os.path.splitext(filename)[0]\n        file_dir = os.path.join(output_dir, name)\n        if os.path.exists(file_dir):\n            shutil.rmtree(file_dir)\n        os.makedirs(file_dir)\n        print(f\"Reading {filename}...\")\n        try:\n            step_index = 1\n            request_index = 1\n            prev_prompt_hash = None\n            with open(filepath, \"rb\") as f:\n                reader = FlowReader(f)\n                for flow in reader.stream():\n                    if not isinstance(flow, HTTPFlow):\n                        continue\n\n                    url = flow.request.pretty_url\n                    if \"/count_token\" in url:\n                        continue\n\n                    # Parse body to check for quota requests\n                    body_text = flow.request.get_text(strict=False)\n                    body_json = None\n                    if body_text:\n                        try:\n                            body_json = json.loads(body_text)\n                            messages = body_json.get(\"messages\", [])\n                            system = body_json.get(\"system\")\n                            if messages and not system:\n                                first_msg = messages[0]\n                                content = first_msg.get(\"content\", \"\")\n                                if isinstance(content, str) and content == \"quota\":\n                                    continue\n                        except json.JSONDecodeError:\n                            pass\n\n                    # For cc: step boundary = system prompt change (checked before writing)\n                    if name == \"cc\" and body_json is not None:\n                        prompt_hash = _system_prompt_hash(body_json, name)\n                        if prompt_hash is not None and prev_prompt_hash is not None and prompt_hash != prev_prompt_hash:\n                            step_index += 1\n                            request_index = 1\n                        if prompt_hash is not None:\n                            prev_prompt_hash = prompt_hash\n\n                    flow_dir = os.path.join(file_dir, str(step_index), str(request_index))\n                    os.makedirs(flow_dir, exist_ok=True)\n\n                    write_request(flow, flow_dir)\n                    write_response(flow, flow_dir)\n                    # Write timing data inline\n                    timing = {}\n                    if flow.request:\n                        timing[\"request_start\"] = flow.request.timestamp_start\n                    if flow.response:\n                        timing[\"response_end\"] = flow.response.timestamp_end\n                    with open(os.path.join(flow_dir, \"timing.json\"), \"w\") as f:\n                        json.dump(timing, f, indent=2)\n                        f.write(\"\\n\")\n\n                    # Extract stop_reason to determine step boundaries\n                    response_raw = \"\"\n                    resp = flow.response\n                    if resp is not None:\n                        response_raw = resp.get_text(strict=False) or \"\"\n                    stop_reason = extract_stop_reason(response_raw)\n\n                    print(f\"  [step {step_index}, req {request_index}] {flow.request.method} {flow.request.pretty_url} ({stop_reason})\")\n\n                    # For vix: step boundary = end_turn stop_reason (checked after writing)\n                    if name != \"cc\":\n                        if stop_reason == \"end_turn\":\n                            step_index += 1\n                            request_index = 1\n                        else:\n                            request_index += 1\n                    else:\n                        request_index += 1\n\n                    total += 1\n        except FlowReadException as e:\n            print(f\"  Skipping {filename}: {e}\")\n        except Exception as e:\n            print(f\"  Skipping {filename}: {e}\")\n\n    print(f\"\\nExported {total} flows to {output_dir}\")\n\n\ndef parse_request_body(request_path: str):"},"name":"edit_file","type":"tool_use"}],"role":"assistant"},{"content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DC23kqvqbJDV8BvjgTZn5a","is_error":false,"content":[{"text":"Edited /workspace/export_flows.py (replaced 1 occurrence).","type":"text"}],"type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},{"content":[{"id":"toolu_017tTZRUVJNwbS92rf1ZVZs8","input":{"command":"cd /workspace \u0026\u0026 /root/.local/pipx/venvs/mitmproxy/bin/python -m pytest test_export_flows.py -v --tb=short 2\u003e\u00261 | tail -15","reason":"Verify Step 4 all tests pass now.","reason_to_use_instead_of_read_file_tool":"N/A","reason_to_use_instead_of_edit_file_tool":"N/A","reason_to_use_instead_of_glob_files_tool":"N/A"},"name":"bash","type":"tool_use"}],"role":"assistant"},{"content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017tTZRUVJNwbS92rf1ZVZs8","is_error":false,"content":[{"text":"test_export_flows.py::TestCalculateCosts::test_calculates_costs PASSED   [ 88%]\ntest_export_flows.py::TestCalculateCosts::test_unknown_model_warns PASSED [ 89%]\ntest_export_flows.py::TestCalculateCosts::test_no_model PASSED           [ 90%]\ntest_export_flows.py::TestExtractFileOps::test_reads_and_writes PASSED   [ 91%]\ntest_export_flows.py::TestExtractFileOps::test_no_ops PASSED             [ 92%]\ntest_export_flows.py::TestExportParsedResponses::test_walks_and_exports PASSED [ 93%]\ntest_export_flows.py::TestRedactFlowFiles::test_no_flow_files PASSED     [ 94%]\ntest_export_flows.py::TestRedactFlowFiles::test_redacts_api_key PASSED   [ 95%]\ntest_export_flows.py::TestExportFlows::test_no_flow_files PASSED         [ 96%]\ntest_export_flows.py::TestExportFlows::test_exports_flows PASSED         [ 97%]\ntest_export_flows.py::TestExportFlows::test_skips_count_token_and_quota PASSED [ 98%]\ntest_export_flows.py::TestSummarizeUsage::test_summarizes PASSED         [ 99%]\ntest_export_flows.py::TestSummarizeUsage::test_skips_non_agent_dirs PASSED [100%]\n\n============================= 102 passed in 0.18s ==============================\n","type":"text"}],"type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},{"content":[{"text":"All 102 pass. Now **Step 5: Create `_usage.py`**. This will contain `parse_request_body`, `extract_usage`, `calculate_costs`, `extract_read_file_whitespace`, `categorize_input_sources`, `extract_file_ops`, `attribute_tokens`, `extract_source_attribution`, and `extract_prompts`:","type":"text"},{"id":"toolu_01T2CjBfUvLGGWZJ6ywiKEhV","input":{"path":"/workspace/_usage.py","content":"import json\nimport os\n\nfrom _models import READ_TOOLS, WRITE_TOOLS, get_pricing, get_canonical_model\nfrom _utils import count_whitespace_stats, _resolve_read_file_name, _get_file_path\nfrom _response_parser import parse_response_content, categorize_output_sources\n\n\ndef parse_request_body(request_path: str):\n    \"\"\"Parse the JSON body from a request.json file. Returns the parsed dict or None.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        with open(request_path, \"r\") as f:\n            return json.load(f)\n    except (json.JSONDecodeError, ValueError):\n        return None\n\n\ndef extract_usage(directory: str):\n    \"\"\"Walk output directory, extract token usage from SSE message_delta events into usage.json.\"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    for dirpath, _dirnames, filenames in os.walk(directory):\n        if \"response_raw.txt\" not in filenames:\n            continue\n\n        response_path = os.path.join(dirpath, \"response_raw.txt\")\n        usage = None\n        with open(response_path, \"r\") as f:\n            content = f.read()\n\n        # Try SSE streaming format: look for message_delta events\n        for line in content.splitlines():\n            line = line.strip()\n            if not line.startswith(\"data: \"):\n                continue\n            payload = line[len(\"data: \"):].strip()\n            if '\"type\":\"message_delta\"' not in payload and '\"type\": \"message_delta\"' not in payload:\n                continue\n            try:\n                data = json.loads(payload)\n                usage = data.get(\"usage\")\n            except json.JSONDecodeError:\n                continue\n\n        # Fallback: non-streaming JSON response (single message object)\n        # The body comes after a blank line following the headers\n        if usage is None:\n            # Find the last {...\"type\":\"message\"...} JSON in the content\n            for line in reversed(content.splitlines()):\n                line = line.strip()\n                if not line.startswith(\"{\"):\n                    continue\n                try:\n                    msg = json.loads(line)\n                    if msg.get(\"type\") == \"message\" and \"usage\" in msg:\n                        usage = msg[\"usage\"]\n                        break\n                except (json.JSONDecodeError, ValueError):\n                    continue\n\n        if usage is None:\n            print(f\"  Warning: no usage found in {response_path}\")\n            continue\n\n        # Keep only the token count fields we need\n        TOKEN_FIELDS = (\"input_tokens\", \"output_tokens\", \"cache_creation_input_tokens\", \"cache_read_input_tokens\")\n        usage = {k: v for k, v in usage.items() if k in TOKEN_FIELDS}\n\n        # Merge timing data if available\n        timing_path = os.path.join(dirpath, \"timing.json\")\n        if os.path.exists(timing_path):\n            with open(timing_path, \"r\") as f:\n                timing = json.load(f)\n            request_start = timing.get(\"request_start\")\n            response_end = timing.get(\"response_end\")\n            timing_block = {}\n            if request_start:\n                timing_block[\"request_start\"] = request_start\n            if response_end:\n                timing_block[\"response_end\"] = response_end\n            if request_start and response_end:\n                timing_block[\"duration_ms\"] = round((response_end - request_start) * 1000)\n            if timing_block:\n                usage[\"timing\"] = timing_block\n            os.remove(timing_path)\n\n        usage_path = os.path.join(dirpath, \"usage.json\")\n        with open(usage_path, \"w\") as f:\n            json.dump(usage, f, indent=2)\n            f.write(\"\\n\")\n        count += 1\n\n    print(f\"\\nExtracted usage for {count} flows\")\n\n\ndef extract_prompts(directory: str):\n    \"\"\"Extract system prompt and first user message from request.json files into per-request markdown files.\"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    for dirpath, _dirnames, filenames in os.walk(directory):\n        if \"request.json\" not in filenames:\n            continue\n\n        request_path = os.path.join(dirpath, \"request.json\")\n\n        body = parse_request_body(request_path)\n        if body is None:\n            print(f\"  Warning: no JSON body found in {request_path}\")\n            continue\n\n        # System prompt: concatenate all text blocks from body[\"system\"]\n        system = body.get(\"system\")\n        if system and isinstance(system, list):\n            texts = [block.get(\"text\", \"\") for block in system if block.get(\"type\") == \"text\"]\n            system_text = \"\\n\\n\".join(t for t in texts if t)\n            if system_text:\n                with open(os.path.join(dirpath, \"system_prompt.md\"), \"w\") as f:\n                    f.write(system_text)\n\n        # First user message: find first message with role==\"user\", concatenate text blocks\n        messages = body.get(\"messages\", [])\n        for msg in messages:\n            if msg.get(\"role\") == \"user\":\n                content = msg.get(\"content\", [])\n                if isinstance(content, list):\n                    texts = [block.get(\"text\", \"\") for block in content if block.get(\"type\") == \"text\"]\n                    user_text = \"\\n\\n\".join(t for t in texts if t)\n                    if user_text:\n                        with open(os.path.join(dirpath, \"first_user_message.md\"), \"w\") as f:\n                            f.write(user_text)\n                break\n\n        count += 1\n\n    print(f\"\\nExtracted prompts for {count} requests\")\n\n\ndef extract_read_file_whitespace(body):\n    \"\"\"Extract whitespace stats from read_file/Read tool results in the request body.\"\"\"\n    ws = {\"line_returns_count\": 0, \"unnecessary_space_count\": 0, \"total_chars\": 0}\n\n    # Build tool_use_id -\u003e tool_name map from assistant messages\n    tool_id_to_name = {}\n    messages = body.get(\"messages\", [])\n    for msg in messages:\n        if msg.get(\"role\") != \"assistant\":\n            continue\n        content = msg.get(\"content\", [])\n        if not isinstance(content, list):\n            continue\n        for block in content:\n            if block.get(\"type\") == \"tool_use\":\n                tool_id_to_name[block.get(\"id\", \"\")] = _resolve_read_file_name(\n                    block.get(\"name\", \"unknown\"), block.get(\"input\", {}))\n\n    for msg in messages:\n        if msg.get(\"role\") != \"user\":\n            continue\n        content = msg.get(\"content\", [])\n        if not isinstance(content, list):\n            continue\n        for block in content:\n            if block.get(\"type\") != \"tool_result\":\n                continue\n            tool_use_id = block.get(\"tool_use_id\", \"\")\n            tool_name = tool_id_to_name.get(tool_use_id, \"unknown\")\n            if not (tool_name.startswith(\"read_file\") or tool_name == \"Read\"):\n                continue\n            result_content = block.get(\"content\", \"\")\n            if isinstance(result_content, str):\n                text_for_ws = result_content\n            elif isinstance(result_content, list):\n                text_for_ws = \"\".join(b.get(\"text\", \"\") for b in result_content)\n            else:\n                text_for_ws = \"\"\n            stats = count_whitespace_stats(text_for_ws)\n            for k in (\"line_returns_count\", \"unnecessary_space_count\", \"total_chars\"):\n                ws[k] += stats[k]\n\n    return ws\n\n\ndef categorize_input_sources(body):\n    \"\"\"Count input characters from tool results and tool use blocks, split by cache position.\n\n    Returns: {\n        \"total_chars\": int,  # total chars of entire request body\n        \"tool_results\": {\"Read\": {\"cache_write_chars\": 0, \"cache_read_chars\": 1234}, ...},\n        \"tool_calls\": {\"Read\": {\"cache_write_chars\": 0, \"cache_read_chars\": 567}, ...},\n    }\n\n    Position logic:\n    - Last user message content ‚Üí cache_write (new content being written to cache)\n    - Second-to-last message (assistant before last user) ‚Üí cache_write for tool_use blocks\n    - Everything else ‚Üí cache_read\n    \"\"\"\n    total_chars = len(json.dumps(body))\n    tool_results = {}\n    tool_calls = {}\n\n    messages = body.get(\"messages\", [])\n\n    # Find last user message index and second-to-last message index\n    last_user_idx = -1\n    for i in range(len(messages) - 1, -1, -1):\n        if messages[i].get(\"role\") == \"user\":\n            last_user_idx = i\n            break\n    second_to_last_idx = last_user_idx - 1 if last_user_idx \u003e 0 else -1\n\n    # Build tool_use_id -\u003e tool_name map from assistant messages\n    tool_id_to_name = {}\n    for msg in messages:\n        if msg.get(\"role\") != \"assistant\":\n            continue\n        content = msg.get(\"content\", [])\n        if not isinstance(content, list):\n            continue\n        for block in content:\n            if block.get(\"type\") == \"tool_use\":\n                tool_id_to_name[block.get(\"id\", \"\")] = _resolve_read_file_name(\n                    block.get(\"name\", \"unknown\"), block.get(\"input\", {}))\n\n    # Collect tool_result chars from user messages\n    for i, msg in enumerate(messages):\n        if msg.get(\"role\") != \"user\":\n            continue\n        content = msg.get(\"content\", [])\n        if not isinstance(content, list):\n            continue\n        is_cache_write = (i == last_user_idx)\n        for block in content:\n            if block.get(\"type\") != \"tool_result\":\n                continue\n            tool_use_id = block.get(\"tool_use_id\", \"\")\n            tool_name = tool_id_to_name.get(tool_use_id, \"unknown\")\n            chars = len(json.dumps(block))\n            if tool_name not in tool_results:\n                tool_results[tool_name] = {\"cache_write_chars\": 0, \"cache_read_chars\": 0}\n            if is_cache_write:\n                tool_results[tool_name][\"cache_write_chars\"] += chars\n            else:\n                tool_results[tool_name][\"cache_read_chars\"] += chars\n\n    # Collect tool_use chars from assistant messages\n    for i, msg in enumerate(messages):\n        if msg.get(\"role\") != \"assistant\":\n            continue\n        content = msg.get(\"content\", [])\n        if not isinstance(content, list):\n            continue\n        is_cache_write = (i == second_to_last_idx)\n        for block in content:\n            if block.get(\"type\") != \"tool_use\":\n                continue\n            tool_name = _resolve_read_file_name(\n                block.get(\"name\", \"unknown\"), block.get(\"input\", {}))\n            chars = len(json.dumps(block))\n            if tool_name not in tool_calls:\n                tool_calls[tool_name] = {\"cache_write_chars\": 0, \"cache_read_chars\": 0}\n            if is_cache_write:\n                tool_calls[tool_name][\"cache_write_chars\"] += chars\n            else:\n                tool_calls[tool_name][\"cache_read_chars\"] += chars\n\n    return {\"total_chars\": total_chars, \"tool_results\": tool_results, \"tool_calls\": tool_calls}\n\n\ndef attribute_tokens(input_sources, output_sources, usage, pricing):\n    \"\"\"Attribute tokens/cost to source categories.\n\n    Input side: raw character counts per tool (no token/cost distribution ‚Äî flawed due to caching).\n    Output side: proportional token/cost distribution (valid since output isn't cached).\n    \"\"\"\n    by_source = {\"input\": {}, \"output\": {}}\n\n    # Input: distribute input tokens proportionally using total_chars as denominator\n    cost_data = usage.get(\"cost\", {})\n    _ci = cost_data.get(\"input\", {})\n    _cw = cost_data.get(\"cache_write\", {})\n    _cr = cost_data.get(\"cache_read\", {})\n    input_tokens = _ci.get(\"tokens\", 0) + _cw.get(\"tokens\", 0) + _cr.get(\"tokens\", 0)\n\n    total_chars = input_sources.get(\"total_chars\", 0)\n\n    def _attribute_input_tool(tool_char_dict):\n        \"\"\"Compute tokens/dollars/chars for a tool given its {cache_write_chars, cache_read_chars}.\"\"\"\n        cw_chars = tool_char_dict.get(\"cache_write_chars\", 0)\n        cr_chars = tool_char_dict.get(\"cache_read_chars\", 0)\n        cw_tokens = round(input_tokens * (cw_chars / total_chars))\n        cr_tokens = round(input_tokens * (cr_chars / total_chars))\n        dollars = (\n            round(cw_tokens * pricing[\"cache_write\"], 6) +\n            round(cr_tokens * pricing[\"cache_read\"], 6)\n        )\n        return {\"tokens\": cw_tokens + cr_tokens, \"dollars\": dollars, \"chars\": cw_chars + cr_chars}\n\n    if total_chars \u003e 0 and input_tokens \u003e 0 and pricing:\n        # Tool results (from user messages)\n        tool_results = input_sources.get(\"tool_results\", {})\n        if tool_results:\n            tr_entry = {}\n            for tool_name, char_dict in tool_results.items():\n                tr_entry[tool_name] = _attribute_input_tool(char_dict)\n            by_source[\"input\"][\"tool_results\"] = tr_entry\n\n        # Tool calls (from assistant messages)\n        tool_calls_input = input_sources.get(\"tool_calls\", {})\n        if tool_calls_input:\n            tc_entry = {}\n            for tool_name, char_dict in tool_calls_input.items():\n                tc_entry[tool_name] = _attribute_input_tool(char_dict)\n            by_source[\"input\"][\"tool_calls\"] = tc_entry\n\n    # Output: distribute output tokens proportionally by character count\n    output_cost_entry = cost_data.get(\"output\", {})\n    output_tokens = output_cost_entry.get(\"tokens\", 0)\n    output_dollars = output_cost_entry.get(\"dollars\", 0.0)\n\n    llm_chars = output_sources.get(\"llm_text\", 0)\n    tc = output_sources.get(\"tool_calls\", {})\n    tc_total_chars = sum(tc.values())\n    total_output_chars = llm_chars + tc_total_chars\n\n    if total_output_chars \u003e 0 and output_tokens \u003e 0:\n        # LLM text\n        llm_frac = llm_chars / total_output_chars\n        by_source[\"output\"][\"llm_text\"] = {\n            \"tokens\": round(output_tokens * llm_frac),\n            \"dollars\": round(output_dollars * llm_frac, 6),\n            \"chars\": llm_chars,\n        }\n\n        # Tool calls\n        tc_frac = tc_total_chars / total_output_chars\n        tc_entry = {\n            \"__total\": {\n                \"tokens\": round(output_tokens * tc_frac),\n                \"dollars\": round(output_dollars * tc_frac, 6),\n                \"chars\": tc_total_chars,\n            }\n        }\n        for tool_name, chars in tc.items():\n            tool_frac = chars / total_output_chars\n            tc_entry[tool_name] = {\n                \"tokens\": round(output_tokens * tool_frac),\n                \"dollars\": round(output_dollars * tool_frac, 6),\n                \"chars\": chars,\n            }\n        by_source[\"output\"][\"tool_calls\"] = tc_entry\n\n    return by_source\n\n\ndef extract_file_ops(body, response_path):\n    \"\"\"Extract file operation stats from request body (reads) and response (writes).\n\n    Returns: {\n        \"input\": {\"unique_files_read\": int, \"total_read_chars\": int, \"per_file\": {path: {\"calls\": int, \"chars\": int}}},\n        \"output\": {\"files_written\": int, \"total_write_chars\": int, \"per_file\": {path: {\"calls\": int, \"chars\": int}}},\n    }\n    \"\"\"\n    # --- Input: files read (from conversation history in request body) ---\n    read_per_file = {}  # path -\u003e {\"calls\": int, \"chars\": int, \"tool_ids\": {id: chars}}\n\n    messages = body.get(\"messages\", [])\n\n    # Build tool_use_id -\u003e (resolved_name, file_path) map from assistant messages\n    tool_id_info = {}\n    for msg in messages:\n        if msg.get(\"role\") != \"assistant\":\n            continue\n        content = msg.get(\"content\", [])\n        if not isinstance(content, list):\n            continue\n        for block in content:\n            if block.get(\"type\") == \"tool_use\":\n                name = _resolve_read_file_name(block.get(\"name\", \"\"), block.get(\"input\", {}))\n                if name in READ_TOOLS:\n                    fp = _get_file_path(block.get(\"input\", {}))\n                    tool_id_info[block.get(\"id\", \"\")] = fp\n\n    # Sum chars from tool_result blocks matching read tools\n    for msg in messages:\n        if msg.get(\"role\") != \"user\":\n            continue\n        content = msg.get(\"content\", [])\n        if not isinstance(content, list):\n            continue\n        for block in content:\n            if block.get(\"type\") != \"tool_result\":\n                continue\n            tool_use_id = block.get(\"tool_use_id\", \"\")\n            if tool_use_id not in tool_id_info:\n                continue\n            fp = tool_id_info[tool_use_id]\n            result_content = block.get(\"content\", \"\")\n            chars = 0\n            if isinstance(result_content, str):\n                chars = len(result_content)\n            elif isinstance(result_content, list):\n                chars = sum(len(b.get(\"text\", \"\")) for b in result_content)\n            if fp:\n                if fp not in read_per_file:\n                    read_per_file[fp] = {\"calls\": 0, \"chars\": 0, \"tool_ids\": {}}\n                read_per_file[fp][\"tool_ids\"][tool_use_id] = chars\n                read_per_file[fp][\"calls\"] = len(read_per_file[fp][\"tool_ids\"])\n                read_per_file[fp][\"chars\"] = sum(read_per_file[fp][\"tool_ids\"].values())\n\n    # --- Output: files written (from response) ---\n    write_per_file = {}  # path -\u003e {\"calls\": int, \"chars\": int, \"tool_ids\": {id: chars}}\n\n    response_blocks = parse_response_content(response_path)\n    for block in response_blocks:\n        if block.get(\"type\") != \"tool_use\":\n            continue\n        name = block.get(\"name\", \"\")\n        if name not in WRITE_TOOLS:\n            continue\n        inp = block.get(\"input\", {})\n        fp = _get_file_path(inp)\n        # Sum content chars: \"content\" for Write/write_file, \"new_string\" for Edit/edit_file\n        chars = 0\n        if name in (\"Write\", \"write_file\"):\n            chars = len(inp.get(\"content\", \"\"))\n        elif name in (\"Edit\", \"edit_file\"):\n            chars = len(inp.get(\"new_string\", \"\"))\n        if fp:\n            block_id = block.get(\"id\", \"\")\n            if fp not in write_per_file:\n                write_per_file[fp] = {\"calls\": 0, \"chars\": 0, \"tool_ids\": {}}\n            write_per_file[fp][\"tool_ids\"][block_id] = chars\n            write_per_file[fp][\"calls\"] = len(write_per_file[fp][\"tool_ids\"])\n            write_per_file[fp][\"chars\"] = sum(write_per_file[fp][\"tool_ids\"].values())\n\n    # Add file_size for each file\n    for pf in (read_per_file, write_per_file):\n        for fp in pf:\n            try:\n                pf[fp][\"file_size\"] = os.path.getsize(fp)\n            except OSError:\n                pf[fp][\"file_size\"] = None\n\n    # Derive aggregate scalars from deduplicated per_file data\n    unique_files_read = len(read_per_file)\n    total_read_chars = sum(v[\"chars\"] for v in read_per_file.values())\n    unique_files_written = len(write_per_file)\n    total_write_chars_dedup = sum(v[\"chars\"] for v in write_per_file.values())\n    total_write_calls = sum(v[\"calls\"] for v in write_per_file.values())\n\n    return {\n        \"input\": {\"unique_files_read\": unique_files_read, \"total_read_chars\": total_read_chars, \"per_file\": read_per_file},\n        \"output\": {\"files_written\": total_write_calls, \"unique_files_written\": unique_files_written, \"total_write_chars\": total_write_chars_dedup, \"per_file\": write_per_file},\n    }\n\n\ndef extract_source_attribution(directory: str):\n    \"\"\"Walk output directory, compute source attribution, read_file whitespace, and file ops.\"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    for dirpath, _dirnames, filenames in os.walk(directory):\n        if \"request.json\" not in filenames or \"usage.json\" not in filenames or \"response_raw.txt\" not in filenames:\n            continue\n\n        request_path = os.path.join(dirpath, \"request.json\")\n        usage_path = os.path.join(dirpath, \"usage.json\")\n        response_path = os.path.join(dirpath, \"response_raw.txt\")\n\n        body = parse_request_body(request_path)\n        if body is None:\n            continue\n\n        with open(usage_path, \"r\") as f:\n            usage = json.load(f)\n\n        # Get model pricing\n        model = body.get(\"model\", \"\")\n        pricing = get_pricing(model) if model else None\n\n        # Compute source attribution\n        input_sources = categorize_input_sources(body)\n        output_sources = categorize_output_sources(response_path)\n        by_source = attribute_tokens(input_sources, output_sources, usage, pricing)\n\n        usage[\"by_source\"] = by_source\n\n        # Compute read_file whitespace\n        usage[\"read_file_whitespace\"] = extract_read_file_whitespace(body)\n\n        # Compute file operations\n        usage[\"file_ops\"] = extract_file_ops(body, response_path)\n\n        with open(usage_path, \"w\") as f:\n            json.dump(usage, f, indent=2)\n            f.write(\"\\n\")\n        count += 1\n\n    print(f\"\\nExtracted source attribution for {count} flows\")\n\n\ndef calculate_costs(directory: str):\n    \"\"\"Walk output directory, compute dollar costs from usage.json and request.json model info.\"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    for dirpath, _dirnames, filenames in os.walk(directory):\n        if \"request.json\" not in filenames or \"usage.json\" not in filenames:\n            continue\n\n        request_path = os.path.join(dirpath, \"request.json\")\n        body = parse_request_body(request_path)\n        if body is None:\n            continue\n\n        model = body.get(\"model\")\n        if not model:\n            continue\n\n        pricing = get_pricing(model)\n        if pricing is None:\n            print(f\"  Warning: unknown model '{model}' in {request_path}, skipping cost calculation\")\n            continue\n\n        usage_path = os.path.join(dirpath, \"usage.json\")\n        with open(usage_path, \"r\") as f:\n            usage = json.load(f)\n\n        tokens_input = usage.get(\"input_tokens\", 0)\n        tokens_cache_write = usage.get(\"cache_creation_input_tokens\", 0)\n        tokens_cache_read = usage.get(\"cache_read_input_tokens\", 0)\n        tokens_output = usage.get(\"output_tokens\", 0)\n        tokens_total = tokens_input + tokens_cache_write + tokens_cache_read + tokens_output\n\n        cost_input = tokens_input * pricing[\"input\"]\n        cost_cache_write = tokens_cache_write * pricing[\"cache_write\"]\n        cost_cache_read = tokens_cache_read * pricing[\"cache_read\"]\n        cost_output = tokens_output * pricing[\"output\"]\n        cost_total = cost_input + cost_cache_write + cost_cache_read + cost_output\n\n        usage[\"cost\"] = {\n            \"input\": {\"tokens\": tokens_input, \"dollars\": round(cost_input, 6)},\n            \"cache_write\": {\"tokens\": tokens_cache_write, \"dollars\": round(cost_cache_write, 6)},\n            \"cache_read\": {\"tokens\": tokens_cache_read, \"dollars\": round(cost_cache_read, 6)},\n            \"output\": {\"tokens\": tokens_output, \"dollars\": round(cost_output, 6)},\n            \"total\": {\"tokens\": tokens_total, \"dollars\": round(cost_total, 6)},\n        }\n\n        # Remove top-level token keys (now redundant with cost entries)\n        for key in (\"input_tokens\", \"cache_creation_input_tokens\", \"cache_read_input_tokens\", \"output_tokens\"):\n            usage.pop(key, None)\n\n        canonical = get_canonical_model(model)\n        if canonical:\n            usage[\"model\"] = canonical\n\n        with open(usage_path, \"w\") as f:\n            json.dump(usage, f, indent=2)\n            f.write(\"\\n\")\n        count += 1\n\n    print(f\"\\nCalculated costs for {count} flows\")\n"},"name":"write_file","type":"tool_use"}],"role":"assistant"},{"content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01T2CjBfUvLGGWZJ6ywiKEhV","is_error":false,"content":[{"text":"Wrote 22855 bytes to /workspace/_usage.py","type":"text"}],"type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},{"content":[{"text":"Now update `export_flows.py` to import from `_usage.py` and remove duplicated code. I'll add the imports and then remove the function bodies:","type":"text"},{"id":"toolu_01AUXhd86y3jQBAef6Lyj3so","input":{"path":"/workspace/export_flows.py","old_string":"from _flow_io import (\n    write_request,\n    write_response,\n)","new_string":"from _flow_io import (\n    write_request,\n    write_response,\n)\nfrom _usage import (\n    parse_request_body,\n    extract_usage,\n    extract_prompts,\n    extract_read_file_whitespace,\n    categorize_input_sources,\n    attribute_tokens,\n    extract_file_ops,\n    extract_source_attribution,\n    calculate_costs,\n)"},"name":"edit_file","type":"tool_use"}],"role":"assistant"},{"content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AUXhd86y3jQBAef6Lyj3so","is_error":false,"content":[{"text":"Edited /workspace/export_flows.py (replaced 1 occurrence).","type":"text"}],"type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},{"content":[{"text":"Now remove all the function definitions that have been moved to `_usage.py`. Let me read the current state:","type":"text"},{"id":"toolu_012KEFWH2UaQXBujCo4sc2gD","input":{"path":"/workspace/export_flows.py","reason":"Check current state to find what to remove for Step 5.","offset":56,"limit":100},"name":"read_file","type":"tool_use"}],"role":"assistant"},{"content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012KEFWH2UaQXBujCo4sc2gD","is_error":false,"content":[{"text":"   56\t    extract_source_attribution,\n   57\t    calculate_costs,\n   58\t)\n   59\t\n   60\t\n   61\tdef redact_flow_files(directory: str):\n   62\t    \"\"\"Redact sensitive headers (API keys) from .flow files in-place.\"\"\"\n   63\t    flow_files = sorted(glob.glob(os.path.join(directory, \"*.flow\")))\n   64\t    if not flow_files:\n   65\t        return\n   66\t\n   67\t    count = 0\n   68\t    for filepath in flow_files:\n   69\t        flows = []\n   70\t        modified = False\n   71\t        try:\n   72\t            with open(filepath, \"rb\") as f:\n   73\t                reader = FlowReader(f)\n   74\t                for flow in reader.stream():\n   75\t                    if isinstance(flow, HTTPFlow):\n   76\t                        for header in _REDACTED_HEADERS:\n   77\t                            if flow.request.headers.get(header):\n   78\t                                flow.request.headers[header] = \"[REDACTED]\"\n   79\t                                modified = True\n   80\t                    flows.append(flow)\n   81\t        except (FlowReadException, Exception) as e:\n   82\t            print(f\"  Skipping {os.path.basename(filepath)}: {e}\")\n   83\t            continue\n   84\t\n   85\t        if modified:\n   86\t            with open(filepath, \"wb\") as f:\n   87\t                writer = FlowWriter(f)\n   88\t                for flow in flows:\n   89\t                    writer.add(flow)\n   90\t            count += 1\n   91\t\n   92\t    print(f\"\\nRedacted API keys in {count} flow files\")\n   93\t\n   94\t\n   95\tdef export_flows(input_dir: str, output_dir: str):\n   96\t    \"\"\"Export .flow files from input_dir into per-flow directories under output_dir.\n   97\t\n   98\t    Directory structure: {agent}/{step_index}/{request_index}/\n   99\t    Steps are delimited by end_turn stop_reason in responses.\n  100\t    \"\"\"\n  101\t    flow_files = sorted(glob.glob(os.path.join(input_dir, \"*.flow\")))\n  102\t    if not flow_files:\n  103\t        print(f\"No *.flow files found in {input_dir}\")\n  104\t        return\n  105\t\n  106\t    total = 0\n  107\t    for filepath in flow_files:\n  108\t        filename = os.path.basename(filepath)\n  109\t        name = os.path.splitext(filename)[0]\n  110\t        file_dir = os.path.join(output_dir, name)\n  111\t        if os.path.exists(file_dir):\n  112\t            shutil.rmtree(file_dir)\n  113\t        os.makedirs(file_dir)\n  114\t        print(f\"Reading {filename}...\")\n  115\t        try:\n  116\t            step_index = 1\n  117\t            request_index = 1\n  118\t            prev_prompt_hash = None\n  119\t            with open(filepath, \"rb\") as f:\n  120\t                reader = FlowReader(f)\n  121\t                for flow in reader.stream():\n  122\t                    if not isinstance(flow, HTTPFlow):\n  123\t                        continue\n  124\t\n  125\t                    url = flow.request.pretty_url\n  126\t                    if \"/count_token\" in url:\n  127\t                        continue\n  128\t\n  129\t                    # Parse body to check for quota requests\n  130\t                    body_text = flow.request.get_text(strict=False)\n  131\t                    body_json = None\n  132\t                    if body_text:\n  133\t                        try:\n  134\t                            body_json = json.loads(body_text)\n  135\t                            messages = body_json.get(\"messages\", [])\n  136\t                            system = body_json.get(\"system\")\n  137\t                            if messages and not system:\n  138\t                                first_msg = messages[0]\n  139\t                                content = first_msg.get(\"content\", \"\")\n  140\t                                if isinstance(content, str) and content == \"quota\":\n  141\t                                    continue\n  142\t                        except json.JSONDecodeError:\n  143\t                            pass\n  144\t\n  145\t                    # For cc: step boundary = system prompt change (checked before writing)\n  146\t                    if name == \"cc\" and body_json is not None:\n  147\t                        prompt_hash = _system_prompt_hash(body_json, name)\n  148\t                        if prompt_hash is not None and prev_prompt_hash is not None and prompt_hash != prev_prompt_hash:\n  149\t                            step_index += 1\n  150\t                            request_index = 1\n  151\t                        if prompt_hash is not None:\n  152\t                            prev_prompt_hash = prompt_hash\n  153\t\n  154\t                    flow_dir = os.path.join(file_dir, str(step_index), str(request_index))\n  155\t                    os.makedirs(flow_dir, exist_ok=True)","type":"text"}],"type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},{"content":[{"id":"toolu_011udJMRG27ibgontfUjCctT","input":{"path":"/workspace/export_flows.py","reason":"See what follows the export_flows function definition.","offset":155,"limit":80},"name":"read_file","type":"tool_use"}],"role":"assistant"},{"content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011udJMRG27ibgontfUjCctT","is_error":false,"content":[{"text":"  155\t                    os.makedirs(flow_dir, exist_ok=True)\n  156\t\n  157\t                    write_request(flow, flow_dir)\n  158\t                    write_response(flow, flow_dir)\n  159\t                    # Write timing data inline\n  160\t                    timing = {}\n  161\t                    if flow.request:\n  162\t                        timing[\"request_start\"] = flow.request.timestamp_start\n  163\t                    if flow.response:\n  164\t                        timing[\"response_end\"] = flow.response.timestamp_end\n  165\t                    with open(os.path.join(flow_dir, \"timing.json\"), \"w\") as f:\n  166\t                        json.dump(timing, f, indent=2)\n  167\t                        f.write(\"\\n\")\n  168\t\n  169\t                    # Extract stop_reason to determine step boundaries\n  170\t                    response_raw = \"\"\n  171\t                    resp = flow.response\n  172\t                    if resp is not None:\n  173\t                        response_raw = resp.get_text(strict=False) or \"\"\n  174\t                    stop_reason = extract_stop_reason(response_raw)\n  175\t\n  176\t                    print(f\"  [step {step_index}, req {request_index}] {flow.request.method} {flow.request.pretty_url} ({stop_reason})\")\n  177\t\n  178\t                    # For vix: step boundary = end_turn stop_reason (checked after writing)\n  179\t                    if name != \"cc\":\n  180\t   